\mute mutes one or more instruments.
Its syntax is the following:

\mute \violin \cello

where \violin and \cello are instruments created with
\insts.init. To mute all instruments, call:

\mute \all

While the sequencer is playing, the instruments are muted
at the start of the next bar. If the sequencer is stopped,
they are muted at once.
To mute instruments immediately, use \mutenow.
To bring them back, use \unmute or \unmutenow.

A muted instrument shows a whole rest in the score and is
hidden in the piano roll.

\mute needs at least one argument, and an argument that
is not an instrument results in an "unknown instrument"
error.
